<http://data.silknow.org/object/3c14f080-3498-39fd-9c89-9a016c070026>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Description: Woven silk and metal thread.\nBlack silk satin ground woven with red silk and metal thread[ silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core] in a repeating pattern of rows of a left-facing boteh infilled with red flower heads and surrounded by large quadrupeds, birds, fish and vases of flowers.\n\nFor similar design see also: T.234-1910 and T.227-1921."@en , "Woven silk fragment"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/3638c744-ed7f-33f7-a5a3-9e8d0eb32392> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/72515b5a-c50a-3d86-a977-d87a6b80131e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Description: Woven silk and metal thread.\nBlack silk satin ground woven with red silk and metal thread[ silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core] in a repeating pattern of rows of a left-facing boteh infilled with red flower heads and surrounded by large quadrupeds, birds, fish and vases of flowers.\n\nFor similar design see also: T.234-1910 and T.227-1921."@en , "Woven silk fragment"@en ;
